        261.02,
        525.98,
        284.6,
        99.96,
        284.6
      ],
      "text": "Subject:- Confirmation on timely submission of Annual Immovable Property Return (AIPR) in the\nproposals seeking input of the Commission on vigilance status of officers for empanelment-reg."
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "text",
      "order": 14,
      "poly": [
        292.74,
        295.54,
        333.2,
        295.54,
        333.2,
        299.75,
        292.74,
        299.75
      ],
      "text": "********"
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "text",
      "order": 15,
      "poly": [
        98.77,
        314.91,
        526.58,
        314.91,
        526.58,
        401.63,
        98.77,
        401.63
      ],
      "text": "Department of Personnel & Training's OM No. 11012/11/2007-Estt.A dated 27.09.2011\n(copy enclosed) conveys the decision of the Govt of India that members of Central Civil\nServices/Posts who fail to submit Annual Immovable Property Returns of the relevant year within\nthe prescribed time limit, would be denied vigilance clearance and they will not be considered for\nempanelment for senior level posts in Government of India. It has inserted sub-para 2(f) which reads\nas under, in the Department of Personnel & Trainings earlier OM No. 11012/11/2007-Estt.A dated\n14.12.2007:"
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "text",
      "order": 16,
      "poly": [
        132.09,
        412.58,
        525.98,
        412.58,
        525.98,
        462.26,
        132.09,
        462.26
      ],
      "text": "\"(f) Vigilance clearance shall be denied to an officer if he fails to submit his annual\nimmovable property return of the previous year by 31st January of the following year, as\nrequired under Government of India decision under Rule 18 of the Central Civil Services\n(Conduct) Rule, 1964.\""
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "text",
      "order": 17,
      "poly": [
        98.18,
        472.36,
        525.38,
        472.36,
        525.38,
        508.57,
        98.18,
        508.57
      ],
      "text": "2. Similarly, as per Rule 16(2) of AIS (Conduct) Rules, 1968, officers are required to submit\nproperty return latest by 31st January of each year, and Department of Personnel & Trainings has\nclarified that those who fail to submit the return on time will be denied vigilance clearance."
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "text",
      "order": 18,
      "poly": [
        98.18,
        519.51,
        525.38,
        519.51,
        525.38,
        593.61,
        98.18,
        593.61
      ],
      "text": "3. It is thus, evident that filing of AIPR on time is a mandatory pre-condition for grant of\nvigilance clearance. So far, the Commission has not been collecting information on AIPR filing while\nconsidering proposals for vigilance clearance, and screening to this effect is left to the concerned\nMinistry/Department/Organization. However, some proposals received by the Commission do\ncontain information on AIPR filing by the concerned officers, and the same is taken in account while\nfinalising input on their vigilance status."
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "text",
      "order": 19,
      "poly": [
